    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. Could you give me some specific examples of high-GI versus low-GI foods? I want to make sure the list I give my client is easy to follow, maybe broken down by food type like grains or fruits.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For grains, white bread and white rice are high-GI, while oats and quinoa are excellent low-GI choices. Among fruits, sugary processed snacks or white bananas tend toward high-GI, whereas apples and berries offer a steady, low-GI sweetness. To keep it simple for your client, focus on replacing refined grains with whole, unrefined alternatives like brown rice or whole-grain breads.",
