    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can you also explain how meal timing or combining these foods with fats or proteins might help? like if they eat a high-GI food with some healthy fats, does that change the overall glycemic response? i'd like to add a section on \"smart swaps\" or strategies for when they can't avoid certain carbs.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, consuming high-GI foods alongside healthy fats or protein significantly blunts the blood sugar spike. Fats and proteins slow down the rate at which stomach contents empty and the digestive enzymes break down carbohydrates. This effectively slows glucose absorption, mitigating the sharp rush associated with high-GI items. Therefore, pairing even a moderate serving of a higher-GI carbohydrate with lean protein or avocado is a powerful strategy to stabilize the glycemic response.",
      "source": "target",
